   "item": "11",
   "section": "Action Calendar – Public Hearings",
   "heading": "Revised External Fixed Surveillance Camera Locations and Vendor Transition",
   "lines": [
    280,
    365
   ],
   "from": "City Manager",
   "contact": "Jennifer Louis, Police, (510) 981-5900",
   "financial_implications": "See report",
   "action": "Action: M/S/Failed (Lunaparra/Tregub) to: 1. Adopt a Resolution with the addition from the City Manager to cite Berkeley Municipal Code Chapter 2.99 in the first resolved clause, removal of the intersection of Telegraph Avenue & Durant Avenue from the list of proposed camera sites, and addition of the following resolved clause: BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED THAT Flock Safety will be directed to not share information, data, or other assets from the External Fixed Video Surveillance Camera program with any personnel or agencies outside of the City of Berkeley, including in response to an administrative subpoena or other request from another government agency, unless compliance is required by court order, or other appropriate directive. Violation of this provision shall be considered grounds for termination of the contract. Flock Safety will inform the City of Berkeley immediately upon receiving any legal or other orders from other jurisdictions. 2. Refer to the City Manager to consider as part of the contracting process the language proposed by Councilmember Barlett related to liquidated damages, and data ownership, storage, and access. Action Calander – New Business Vote: Ayes – Bartlett, Tregub; Noes – Kesarwani, Taplin; O’Keefe, Blackaby, Humbert, Ishii; Abstain – Lunaparra. Action: 30 speakers. M/S/Carried (Humbert/Blackaby) to adopt Resolution No. 71,698–N.S. with the addition from the City Manager to cite Berkeley Municipal Code Chapter 2.99 in the first resolved clause, and addition of the following resolved clause: BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED THAT Flock Safety will be directed to not share information, data, or other assets from the External Fixed Video Surveillance Camera program with any personnel or agencies outside of the City of Berkeley, including in response to an administrative subpoena or other request from another government agency, unless compliance is required by court order, or other appropriate directive. Violation of this provision shall be considered grounds for termination of the contract. Flock Safety will inform the City of Berkeley immediately upon receiving any legal or other orders from other jurisdictions. Vote: Ayes – Kesarwani, Taplin, Bartlett, Tregub, O’Keefe, Blackaby, Humbert, Ishii; Noes – Lunaparra; Abstain – None.",
   "speakers": 30,
   "attribution": [],
